<title>BRAZIL: Brazil federal job cut plan may cost 900 mln reais.</title>
<headline>Brazil federal job cut plan may cost 900 mln reais.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's government expects a voluntary redundancy plan for federal government workers to cost 900 million reais and to affect 30,000 civil servants, said a spokesman for the Administration Ministry.</p>
<p>&quot;The National Treasury has allocated 900 million reais for the program and we expect about five percent of the total federal payroll to apply, which is about 30,000,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>The federal government Tuesday unveiled a voluntary job cut plan that could be taken up by nearly 320,000 of the 546,000 civil servants.</p>
<p>--Michael Christie, Brasilia Newsroom, 55-61-223-0358</p>
</text>
